# Mobile frozen — desktop-only by default

## Policy

Mobile layouts for the registration hub and main site are **frozen**. Treat current mobile behavior and styles as locked.

Unless the user **explicitly** asks for mobile (or “all breakpoints”), do **not** change:

- Rules inside `@media (max-width: 767px)`
- Mobile-only markup, classes (e.g. `u-mob-only`), or JS branches keyed to `max-width: 767px` / `matchMedia('(min-width:768px)')` when the change affects mobile UX

## Default for new requests

Put layout, typography, hero, accordion, header/footer, and visual tweaks in **`@media (min-width: 768px)`** (or new desktop-only blocks). Prefer overriding inside the existing desktop block (~line 227 in `register/index.html`) instead of editing shared base rules that would shift mobile.

## When editing shared (unscoped) CSS

If a change must touch global selectors, duplicate or scope so **computed styles at ≤767px stay identical** to the frozen state. Verify mentally or in devtools that mobile is unchanged.

## Exceptions

- Bug fixes that break mobile functionally (forms, links, OTP, API)
- User says “mobile”, “phone”, “all screens”, or “responsive”

Breakpoint: **768px** (`767` max / `768` min), matching existing `register/index.html`.